    },
    {
      "text": "Fig. 2.",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        228.76573181152344,
        72.6314468383789,
        236.50668334960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Example of N \u0002 1 D 4 ancestral lineages generated by a conditional SMC algorithm for N D 5 and",
      "bbox": [
        81.00005340576172,
        228.07949829101562,
        443.431640625,
        236.50668334960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "T D3 conditional on X2",
      "bbox": [
        48.0897216796875,
        235.83883666992188,
        133.0819854736328,
        245.47280883789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:3 and B2",
      "bbox": [
        129.06396484375,
        235.83883666992188,
        167.65957641601562,
        248.65304565429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:3",
      "bbox": [
        163.30690002441406,
        242.05657958984375,
        172.72360229492188,
        248.32308959960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sophisticated algorithms have been proposed in the literature to improve on such a basic scheme;",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        261.48907470703125,
        443.6049499511719,
        270.7243957519531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "see Cappé et al. (2005) or Doucet and Johansen (2009) for recent reviews. Such techniques essen-",
      "bbox": [
        48.089698791503906,
        273.4441833496094,
        443.60595703125,
        282.67950439453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tially fall into two categories:",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        285.3992919921875,
        170.24111938476562,
        294.6346130371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(a) techniques aiming at reducing the variance that is introduced by the resampling step of",
      "bbox": [
        57.98057556152344,
        303.1865234375,
        443.6067810058594,
        312.4218444824219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the SMC algorithm such as the popular residual and stratiﬁed resampling procedures",
      "bbox": [
        74.98872375488281,
        315.1416320800781,
        443.60888671875,
        324.376953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(see Liu (2001), chapter 3, and Kitagawa (1996)) and",
      "bbox": [
        74.98872375488281,
        327.09674072265625,
        296.96533203125,
        336.3320617675781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(b) techniquesaimingatﬁghtingtheso-calleddegeneracyphenomenonwhichinclude,among",
      "bbox": [
        57.98057556152344,
        339.0518493652344,
        443.6049499511719,
        348.28717041015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "others, the auxiliary particle ﬁlter (Pitt and Shephard, 1999) or the resample–move algo-",
      "bbox": [
        74.98872375488281,
        351.0069580078125,
        443.60882568359375,
        360.2422790527344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rithm (Gilks and Berzuini, 2001).",
      "bbox": [
        74.98872375488281,
        362.9620666503906,
        214.98312377929688,
        372.1973876953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Popular advanced resampling schemes can be used within the PMCMC framework—more",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        380.7492980957031,
        443.6039733886719,
        389.984619140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "details on the technical conditions that are required by such schemes are given in Section",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        392.70440673828125,
        443.60296630859375,
        401.9397277832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4.1. Roughly speaking these conditions require some form of exchangeability of the parti-",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        404.6595153808594,
        443.6008605957031,
        413.89483642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cles. Most known advanced SMC techniques falling into category (b) will also lead to valid",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        416.6146240234375,
        443.60382080078125,
        425.8499450683594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PMCMC algorithms. Such valid techniques can in fact be easily identiﬁed in practice but this",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        428.5697326660156,
        443.6097106933594,
        437.8050537109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "requires us to consider the more general PMCMC framework that is developed in Section",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        440.5248718261719,
        443.61083984375,
        449.76019287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4.1.",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        452.47998046875,
        63.45203399658203,
        461.7153015136719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2.5.2.",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        477.8846130371094,
        71.1332015991211,
        487.0502014160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Using all the particles",
      "bbox": [
        81.0958023071289,
        477.8846130371094,
        170.57984924316406,
        487.0502014160156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A possible criticism of the PMCMC updates is that they require the generation of N particles",
      "bbox": [
        48.08970642089844,
        489.9393615722656,
        443.6098937988281,
        499.1746826171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "at each iteration of the MCMC algorithm to propose a single sample. It is shown in theorem",
      "bbox": [
        48.089752197265625,
        501.8945007324219,
        443.60693359375,
        511.12982177734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6 in Section 4.6 that it is possible to reuse all the particles that are generated in the PIMH,",
      "bbox": [
        48.089752197265625,
        513.8495483398438,
        443.6089782714844,
        523.0848999023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
